WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.192
Project A creates a contact-data quality view.

00:00:03.192 --> 00:00:06.612
The raw name remains visible beside the cleaned name.

00:00:06.612 --> 00:00:10.647
The email is normalized and checked for a teaching-level valid shape.

00:00:10.647 --> 00:00:14.472
The address uses a documented abbreviation replacement.

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:19.622
This design is audit-friendly because the transformation does not hide the original values.

00:00:19.622 --> 00:00:25.117
Connect this idea to a CRM standardizing names, emails, and phone numbers.

00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:30.312
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:30.312 --> 00:00:37.172
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:37.172 --> 00:00:42.317
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:47.680
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
